WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.440
- I'm just saying, I
heard though that Daniel,

00:00:02.440 --> 00:00:04.760
did you just, right before the pandemic,

00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:07.060
did you just say you're
giving up on video games?

00:00:07.060 --> 00:00:09.656
And do you think that
was maybe poor timing?

00:00:09.656 --> 00:00:11.140
(laughs)

00:00:11.140 --> 00:00:14.170
- No, I gave up video games a while ago

00:00:14.170 --> 00:00:19.153
because if I do video games, I
do nothing else with my life.

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:24.420
I have done very little
of actual productive value

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:25.800
while being in quarantine.
(laughs)

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:27.540
But I know that if I did play video games,

00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:30.350
it would be all that I did all the time.

00:00:30.350 --> 00:00:33.140
And this way, I can
give myself the illusion

00:00:33.140 --> 00:00:36.640
of being productive when I
read a book for 10 seconds

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:38.920
or whatever it is.
(laughs)

00:00:38.920 --> 00:00:40.750
The thing that has really
been getting us through

00:00:40.750 --> 00:00:44.310
this quarantine has been large Lego sets,

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:47.602
which take up a lot of
time, are very meditative.

00:00:47.602 --> 00:00:48.790
- Wait, what did you put together?

00:00:48.790 --> 00:00:50.220
What's your large Lego set?

00:00:50.220 --> 00:00:51.053
What is that?

00:00:51.053 --> 00:00:54.010
- Well, we made a "Jurassic Park" one

00:00:54.010 --> 00:00:54.850
which is very big.
- What?

00:00:54.850 --> 00:00:57.030
- And we just started a
"Stranger Things" one,

00:00:57.030 --> 00:00:58.160
which is half built.

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:00.920
But it's very cool, 'cause
it's got two levels to it.

00:01:00.920 --> 00:01:03.030
It's the normal world and
then the upside-down world

00:01:03.030 --> 00:01:04.420
that's built upside down on top.

00:01:04.420 --> 00:01:05.790
It's very cool, we don't know how

00:01:05.790 --> 00:01:06.950
we're gonna put it all together yet.

00:01:06.950 --> 00:01:08.270
It could all fall apart.

00:01:08.270 --> 00:01:10.143
- That's amazing, I feel you.

00:01:12.370 --> 00:01:14.450
Jane, have you found any hobbies

00:01:14.450 --> 00:01:15.770
or anything to keep you busy right now,

00:01:15.770 --> 00:01:17.800
other than teaching your child?

00:01:17.800 --> 00:01:20.500
- Yeah, other than struggling
through the third grade.

00:01:21.770 --> 00:01:23.950
I have taken up ukulele

00:01:23.950 --> 00:01:26.390
- What?
- during quarantine. (laughs)

00:01:26.390 --> 00:01:27.640
- Are you serious?

00:01:27.640 --> 00:01:30.540
- It's always been this thing
I wanted to be able to play,

00:01:30.540 --> 00:01:32.680
I guess just 'cause it
seems easy to carry around.

00:01:32.680 --> 00:01:34.905
It's a lot lighter than a harp.

00:01:34.905 --> 00:01:37.730
(laughs)

00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:40.070
So I've started, I've
only taken three classes

00:01:40.070 --> 00:01:41.500
'cause as I say, I had to get in the swing

00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:43.750
of the school thing first,
the distance learning.

00:01:43.750 --> 00:01:45.100
And then, I got to this.

00:01:45.100 --> 00:01:46.900
So it's been fun.

00:01:46.900 --> 00:01:49.793
I can't play any songs
yet, just a few chords.

00:01:51.610 --> 00:01:53.633
It's definitely my quarantine hobby.

00:01:54.790 --> 00:01:56.260
- You're not talented enough?

00:01:56.260 --> 00:01:57.240
That's just been rude.

00:01:57.240 --> 00:01:58.280
That's just being greedy

00:01:58.280 --> 00:02:00.240
with your talent.
(laughs)

00:02:00.240 --> 00:02:01.073
That's so cool!

00:02:01.073 --> 00:02:02.553
The ukulele is so cool.

